    "macOS has no way to directly ask an app to open a new window, so this button brings the app to the front and sends it the standard ⌘N keyboard shortcut.\n\nMost apps open a new window with ⌘N, but some use it for something else, like a new document, note, or message, and a few ignore it entirely. Whatever the app does when you press ⌘N yourself is what this button will do." : {
      "comment" : "Preview action enablement alert message",
      "localizations" : {
        "af" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "macOS has no way to directly ask an app to open a new window, so this button brings the app to the front and sends it the standard ⌘N keyboard shortcut.\n\nMost apps open a new window with ⌘N, but some use it for something else, like a new document, note, or message, and a few ignore it entirely. Whatever the app does when you press ⌘N yourself is what this button will do."
          }
