    "Your widgets were updated because the widget system was redesigned.\n\nWidgets used to be stored as global shelves. They now live as reusable Widget Stack definitions that you configure once, then add to whichever dock profiles should use them.\n\nWe added your existing widgets to %lld enabled dock profile(s). In Taskbar mode they sit at the dock's leading and trailing edges; in Floating mode they appear inline at the start and end of the dock. The Trash is now a built-in element at the end of the dock; you can turn it off with \"Show Trash\" in Settings > Dock.\n\nYou can review or edit the reusable stacks in Settings > Widgets, then add or remove them from each profile in the Dock Profile editor." : {
      "comment" : "Alert message explaining widget stack port after redesign",
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "af" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Your widgets were updated because the widget system was redesigned.\n\nWidgets used to be stored as global shelves. They now live as reusable Widget Stack definitions that you configure once, then add to whichever dock profiles should use them.\n\nWe added your existing widgets to %lld enabled dock profile(s). In Taskbar mode they sit at the dock's leading and trailing edges; in Floating mode they appear inline at the start and end of the dock. The Trash is now a built-in element at the end of the dock; you can turn it off with \"Show Trash\" in Settings > Dock.\n\nYou can review or edit the reusable stacks in Settings > Widgets, then add or remove them from each profile in the Dock Profile editor."
          }
        },
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Your widgets were updated because the widget system was redesigned.\n\nWidgets used to be stored as global shelves. They now live as reusable Widget Stack definitions that you configure once, then add to whichever dock profiles should use them.\n\nWe added your existing widgets to %lld enabled dock profile(s). In Taskbar mode they sit at the dock's leading and trailing edges; in Floating mode they appear inline at the start and end of the dock. The Trash is now a built-in element at the end of the dock; you can turn it off with \"Show Trash\" in Settings > Dock.\n\nYou can review or edit the reusable stacks in Settings > Widgets, then add or remove them from each profile in the Dock Profile editor."
          }
        },
        "ca" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Your widgets were updated because the widget system was redesigned.\n\nWidgets used to be stored as global shelves. They now live as reusable Widget Stack definitions that you configure once, then add to whichever dock profiles should use them.\n\nWe added your existing widgets to %lld enabled dock profile(s). In Taskbar mode they sit at the dock's leading and trailing edges; in Floating mode they appear inline at the start and end of the dock. The Trash is now a built-in element at the end of the dock; you can turn it off with \"Show Trash\" in Settings > Dock.\n\nYou can review or edit the reusable stacks in Settings > Widgets, then add or remove them from each profile in the Dock Profile editor."
          }
        },
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Your widgets were updated because the widget system was redesigned.\n\nWidgets used to be stored as global shelves. They now live as reusable Widget Stack definitions that you configure once, then add to whichever dock profiles should use them.\n\nWe added your existing widgets to %lld enabled dock profile(s). In Taskbar mode they sit at the dock's leading and trailing edges; in Floating mode they appear inline at the start and end of the dock. The Trash is now a built-in element at the end of the dock; you can turn it off with \"Show Trash\" in Settings > Dock.\n\nYou can review or edit the reusable stacks in Settings > Widgets, then add or remove them from each profile in the Dock Profile editor."
          }
        },
        "da" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Your widgets were updated because the widget system was redesigned.\n\nWidgets used to be stored as global shelves. They now live as reusable Widget Stack definitions that you configure once, then add to whichever dock profiles should use them.\n\nWe added your existing widgets to %lld enabled dock profile(s). In Taskbar mode they sit at the dock's leading and trailing edges; in Floating mode they appear inline at the start and end of the dock. The Trash is now a built-in element at the end of the dock; you can turn it off with \"Show Trash\" in Settings > Dock.\n\nYou can review or edit the reusable stacks in Settings > Widgets, then add or remove them from each profile in the Dock Profile editor."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ihre Widgets wurden aktualisiert, weil das Widget-System neu gestaltet wurde.\n\nWidgets wurden bisher als globale Ablagen gespeichert. Jetzt sind sie als wiederverwendbare Widget-Stapel definiert, die Sie einmal konfigurieren und dann den Dock-Profilen hinzufügen, die sie verwenden sollen.\n\nWir haben Ihre vorhandenen Widgets zu %lld aktivierten Dock-Profil(en) hinzugefügt. Im Taskleistenmodus befinden sie sich an Vorder- und Hinterkante des Docks; im schwebenden Modus erscheinen sie direkt am Anfang und Ende des Docks. Der Papierkorb ist jetzt ein integriertes Element am Ende des Docks; Sie können ihn mit &quot;Papierkorb anzeigen&quot; in Einstellungen &gt; Dock deaktivieren.\n\nSie können die wiederverwendbaren Stapel in Einstellungen &gt; Widgets prüfen oder bearbeiten und sie anschließend im Dock-Profil-Editor jedem Profil hinzufügen oder daraus entfernen."
          }
        },
        "el" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Your widgets were updated because the widget system was redesigned.\n\nWidgets used to be stored as global shelves. They now live as reusable Widget Stack definitions that you configure once, then add to whichever dock profiles should use them.\n\nWe added your existing widgets to %lld enabled dock profile(s). In Taskbar mode they sit at the dock's leading and trailing edges; in Floating mode they appear inline at the start and end of the dock. The Trash is now a built-in element at the end of the dock; you can turn it off with \"Show Trash\" in Settings > Dock.\n\nYou can review or edit the reusable stacks in Settings > Widgets, then add or remove them from each profile in the Dock Profile editor."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
