        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Your widgets were updated because the widget system was redesigned.\n\nWidgets used to be stored as global shelves. They now live as reusable Widget Stack definitions that you configure once, then add to whichever dock profiles should use them.\n\nWe added your existing widgets to %lld enabled dock profile(s). In Taskbar mode they sit at the dock's leading and trailing edges; in Floating mode they appear inline at the start and end of the dock. The Trash is now a built-in element at the end of the dock; you can turn it off with \"Show Trash\" in Settings > Dock.\n\nYou can review or edit the reusable stacks in Settings > Widgets, then add or remove them from each profile in the Dock Profile editor."
          }
        },
        "nb" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Your widgets were updated because the widget system was redesigned.\n\nWidgets used to be stored as global shelves. They now live as reusable Widget Stack definitions that you configure once, then add to whichever dock profiles should use them.\n\nWe added your existing widgets to %lld enabled dock profile(s). In Taskbar mode they sit at the dock's leading and trailing edges; in Floating mode they appear inline at the start and end of the dock. The Trash is now a built-in element at the end of the dock; you can turn it off with \"Show Trash\" in Settings > Dock.\n\nYou can review or edit the reusable stacks in Settings > Widgets, then add or remove them from each profile in the Dock Profile editor."
          }
        },
        "nl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Je widgets zijn bijgewerkt omdat het widgetsysteem opnieuw is ontworpen.\n\nVoorheen werden widgets opgeslagen als globale planken. Ze worden nu opgeslagen als herbruikbare widgetstapels die je één keer configureert en vervolgens kan toevoegen aan de Dock-profielen waarin je ze ze wilt gebruiken.\n\nWe hebben je bestaande widgets toegevoegd aan %lld ingeschakelde Dock-profiel(en). In de taakbalkmodus staan ze aan de voor- en achterkant van het Dock; in de zwevende modus verschijnen ze inline aan het begin en einde van het Dock. De prullenmand is nu een ingebouwd element aan het einde van het Dock; je kunt deze uitschakelen met 'Prullenmand weergeven' in Instellingen ▸ Dock.\n\nJe kunt de herbruikbare stapels bekijken of bewerken in Instellingen ▸ Widgets, en ze vervolgens toevoegen aan of verwijderen uit elk profiel in de Dock-profiel-editor."
          }
        },
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Twoje widżety zostały zaktualizowane, ponieważ system widżetów został przeprojektowany.\n\nWidżety były wcześniej przechowywane jako globalne półki. Teraz działają jako definicje Stosów widżetów wielokrotnego użytku, które konfigurujesz raz, a potem dodajesz do profili Docka, które mają ich używać.\n\nDodaliśmy istniejące widżety do włączonych profili Docka. Liczba profili: %lld. W trybie paska zadań znajdują się przy początkowej i końcowej krawędzi Docka; w trybie pływającym pojawiają się w linii na początku i końcu Docka. Kosz jest teraz wbudowanym elementem na końcu Docka; możesz go wyłączyć opcją „Pokaż Kosz” w Ustawienia > Dock.\n\nMożesz przejrzeć lub edytować stosy wielokrotnego użytku w Ustawienia > Widżety, a potem dodawać je do każdego profilu albo usuwać je z profili w edytorze profilu Docka."
          }
        },
        "pt" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Your widgets were updated because the widget system was redesigned.\n\nWidgets used to be stored as global shelves. They now live as reusable Widget Stack definitions that you configure once, then add to whichever dock profiles should use them.\n\nWe added your existing widgets to %lld enabled dock profile(s). In Taskbar mode they sit at the dock's leading and trailing edges; in Floating mode they appear inline at the start and end of the dock. The Trash is now a built-in element at the end of the dock; you can turn it off with \"Show Trash\" in Settings > Dock.\n\nYou can review or edit the reusable stacks in Settings > Widgets, then add or remove them from each profile in the Dock Profile editor."
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Your widgets were updated because the widget system was redesigned.\n\nWidgets used to be stored as global shelves. They now live as reusable Widget Stack definitions that you configure once, then add to whichever dock profiles should use them.\n\nWe added your existing widgets to %lld enabled dock profile(s). In Taskbar mode they sit at the dock's leading and trailing edges; in Floating mode they appear inline at the start and end of the dock. The Trash is now a built-in element at the end of the dock; you can turn it off with \"Show Trash\" in Settings > Dock.\n\nYou can review or edit the reusable stacks in Settings > Widgets, then add or remove them from each profile in the Dock Profile editor."
          }
        },
        "ro" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Your widgets were updated because the widget system was redesigned.\n\nWidgets used to be stored as global shelves. They now live as reusable Widget Stack definitions that you configure once, then add to whichever dock profiles should use them.\n\nWe added your existing widgets to %lld enabled dock profile(s). In Taskbar mode they sit at the dock's leading and trailing edges; in Floating mode they appear inline at the start and end of the dock. The Trash is now a built-in element at the end of the dock; you can turn it off with \"Show Trash\" in Settings > Dock.\n\nYou can review or edit the reusable stacks in Settings > Widgets, then add or remove them from each profile in the Dock Profile editor."
          }
        },
        "ru" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ваши виджеты были обновлены, потому что система виджетов была переработана.\n\nРаньше виджеты хранились как глобальные полки. Теперь они существуют как повторно используемые определения стопок виджетов, которые вы настраиваете один раз, а затем добавляете в те профили дока, которые должны их использовать.\n\nМы добавили ваши существующие виджеты в %lld включённых профилей дока. В режиме панели задач они располагаются у левого и правого краёв дока; в плавающем режиме они отображаются встроенно в начале и конце дока. Корзина теперь является встроенным элементом в конце дока; вы можете отключить её с помощью «Show Trash» в Settings &gt; Dock.\n\nВы можете просмотреть или отредактировать повторно используемые стопки в Settings &gt; Widgets, затем добавить или удалить их из каждого профиля в редакторе профиля дока."
          }
        },
        "sr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Your widgets were updated because the widget system was redesigned.\n\nWidgets used to be stored as global shelves. They now live as reusable Widget Stack definitions that you configure once, then add to whichever dock profiles should use them.\n\nWe added your existing widgets to %lld enabled dock profile(s). In Taskbar mode they sit at the dock's leading and trailing edges; in Floating mode they appear inline at the start and end of the dock. The Trash is now a built-in element at the end of the dock; you can turn it off with \"Show Trash\" in Settings > Dock.\n\nYou can review or edit the reusable stacks in Settings > Widgets, then add or remove them from each profile in the Dock Profile editor."
          }
        },
        "sv" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Your widgets were updated because the widget system was redesigned.\n\nWidgets used to be stored as global shelves. They now live as reusable Widget Stack definitions that you configure once, then add to whichever dock profiles should use them.\n\nWe added your existing widgets to %lld enabled dock profile(s). In Taskbar mode they sit at the dock's leading and trailing edges; in Floating mode they appear inline at the start and end of the dock. The Trash is now a built-in element at the end of the dock; you can turn it off with \"Show Trash\" in Settings > Dock.\n\nYou can review or edit the reusable stacks in Settings > Widgets, then add or remove them from each profile in the Dock Profile editor."
